<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">company inventory</ansi>

One screen for everything your company carries.

  <ansi fg="command">company inventory</ansi> (or <ansi fg="command">company inv</ansi>)

It shows:

  - The company's load against its capacity, and how much of that the
    horses carry (<ansi fg="command">help cargo</ansi>).
  - Assigned packs: carrier, capacity and availability. Fallen and away
    carriers contribute no capacity (<ansi fg="command">help pack</ansi>).
  - All unworn items once in shared cargo with exact item references.
    A partly used item shows its uses left, like
    <ansi fg="yellow">waterskin (3 of 5)</ansi>.
  - Your horses and their saddles (<ansi fg="command">help mount</ansi>).
  - The shared cargo and its weight.

For one companion in full, type <ansi fg="command">company gear [member]</ansi>; for the load and
capacity split, <ansi fg="command">cargo</ansi>. <ansi fg="command">company equip</ansi> follows each companion's class: it
refuses a shield or weapon the class isn't taught (<ansi fg="command">help shields</ansi>) and warns
about armor heavier than its training (<ansi fg="command">help armor</ansi>).

In the web client, Company Inventory shows shared Cargo, treasury, supplies
and containers. Worn gear is not listed there, since it does not count toward
the load: it is under Character > Gear (<ansi fg="command">help companion-gear</ansi>). Tabs above the
cargo sort it: All (everything), Equipment, Potions, Food & drink, Materials
and Other. A tab with nothing in it is hidden, and each shows how many items
it holds. Tap a cargo item to look at it, compare it for a member, or equip it.
In Character > Gear, choose a member, select a slot and a compatible item for a
Current → After preview; equip or preview removal there (<ansi fg="command">help webclient</ansi>).

See also: <ansi fg="command">help cargo</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help mount</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help company meal</ansi>,
<ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help inventory</ansi>.

Shared cargo and deliberate equipment assignment: <ansi fg="command">help equipment</ansi>.
Pooled gold: <ansi fg="command">help treasury</ansi>. Battle spoils: <ansi fg="command">help loot</ansi>.
